      plan: 'Begin at the Old Bridge Gate and follow Steingasse to Market Square. Continue along Hauptstraße towards University Square, with short detours to the Old University and Student Jail. Extend the route to Karlsplatz and return near the river.',
      photo: 'Frame the church with neighbouring houses from Market Square; side lanes reveal façades and cobblestones. Mornings tend to be quieter on the main street.',
      transport: 'Much of the centre is pedestrianised. Use bus or tram to the edge of Old Town and continue on foot; parking garages are outside the central lanes.',
      faq: [['Is Old Town free?', 'Public streets and squares are free to explore; museums and guided tours may charge admission.'], ['How long is a walk?', 'Allow about 60–120 minutes for the core route, longer with museum visits.'], ['Can I drive through?', 'Many central sections are pedestrian areas; follow local access restrictions.']],
